        <div class="jcBand">
            <div id="pnlJobDescription">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Why Join DHCS? </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">The Department of Health Care Services (DHCS) is the backbone of California’s health care safety net. Our success is made possible by the hard work of more than 4,800 DHCS team members and through collaboration with the federal government and other state agencies, counties, and partners for the care of low-income families, children, pregnant women, older adults, and persons with disabilities. This is an exciting opportunity to join our diverse team in the following role. If you are interested in joining our team, apply today! </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">&nbsp;</span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">About this Role:</span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">The Associate Bond Analyst works independently performing a wide variety of difficult and complex financial and accounting transactions such as analyzing, interpreting and implementing GASB pronouncements; &nbsp;reconciling and preparing Generally Accepted Accounting Principle (GAAP) Financial Statements, Budgetary/ Legal Basis financial statements, implementing Governmental Accounting Standard Board (GASB) pronouncements and contributing to day-to-day cash and debt management of the $4.393 billion the Department of Health Care Services (DHCS) Behavioral Health Treatment (BHT) General Obligation bond portfolio. This includes researching, analyzing, preparing bond accounting entries and providing recommendations or alternatives regarding the complex financing, accounting and compliance issues of BHT bond fund portfolio.</span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">This advertisement is posted as&nbsp;until&nbsp;filled. Applications will be reviewed on the 1st and 15th of every month, and selections can be made.</span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">This limited-term position may be extended up to 24 months or may become permanent pending budget approval.</span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">This is a re-advertisement of JC-455328. If you previously applied under JC-455328, you would need to re-apply under this new Job Control,&nbsp;JC-460496&nbsp;in order to be considered.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">Have questions and/or need assistance?&nbsp;</span><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">Contact&nbsp;</span><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; color: #0000ff;">Recruit@dhcs.ca.gov</span><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">, we are here to help walk you through the state hiring process!</span></p><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=25917342&name=Bond-DutyStatement-AAA.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
</div>

            <div id="pnlWorkingConditions">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Working Conditions</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <ul style="margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px;">
